These subsets normalize upstream fields into JSONL, sample records with seed
407, and add final-answer formatting instructions to capability inputs.
See data/README.md and data/refusal/manifest.json for source URLs and hashes.

Direction prompts are generated using Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and its uncensored
variant. Recorded served names are qwen3.8-flash-next-uncensored for harmful
generation and qwen3.8-flash-next for benign generation and filtering. The
manifest does not record fixed model revisions or a separate license grant for
the generated prompts. See data/direction/manifest.json and data/README.md.

The activation collector uses llama.cpp, licensed under the MIT License:
https://github.com/ishikawa/llama.cpp
https://github.com/ishikawa/llama.cpp/blob/ddf120c50a8acfbf873c16cb070c2b5e4bb6a2fe/LICENSE
Its build links llama.cpp libraries and uses its common chat/template interfaces,
GGML interfaces, vendored JSON headers and SHA-256 implementation. These external
sources are supplied by the llama.cpp source tree rather than bundled here.

The model release under hf/ uses MIT as declared by zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash.
